	(text "Mains zero-cross and presence detector"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.67 201.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "104d5b6a-4c58-5788-9de8-a8b2f984088c")
	)
	(text "CURRENT MEASUREMENT (hardware design section 10).\nR37 0.1R 1 % 2 W carries the return current of every valve: ISNS is the common T1 node of all triacs.\n0.23 W at 1.5 A rms. A 20 A short lifts ISNS to 2.8 V for a half-cycle; the 7.5k input resistors\nkeep that inside the op-amp's 2 mA input limit.\nU8A: gain 10k / 7.5k = 1.333, 133.3 mV/A, linear to 5.8 A peak.  U8B: 49.9k / 7.5k = 6.653,\n665.3 mV/A, linear to 1.17 A peak. Both outputs are AC waveforms centred on VB, about 0.79 V.\nFirmware takes the rms over 100 ms windows; there is no rectifier. C26 to C29: 15 kHz.\nR46 with C30 and R47 with C31: 1.6 kHz at the ADC pins; place the capacitors at module pins 39, 38.\n\nLAYOUT: Kelvin connections. R38 and R42 go to the ISNS pad of R37, R40 and R44 to its ground pad\nwith their own trace, not to the ground plane. Keep this block away from L1, the display clock\nand the antenna."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 279.4 132.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c944cc96-b3bf-5e0e-8377-b56197197f75")
	)
	(text "THRESHOLDS (section 9.1). VH 1.425 V, VB 0.806 V, VL 0.188 V: trip at 0.619 V / 0.1333 V/A = 4.64 A peak.\nZERO-CROSS (section 11). R55, R88, R56 divide AC_L by 12. D9 clamps; R88 halves the clamped level so\nthe LM2901 input stays above -0.3 V (-0.18 V at -20 C and 32 VAC). U6D compares with VL; R57 adds\n30 mV of hysteresis. AC_ZC is a square wave at mains frequency, high while AC_L is above about 2.3 V.\nNo edge for 25 ms means the 24 VAC is gone. R55 is a 1206 part rated 200 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 241.3 205.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "daf76765-bf20-5737-b2c3-3e10b31f561e")
	)
	(text "Shunt and two difference amplifiers, both biased at VB"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
